# Build context hygiene — mirrors .gitignore.
# Most importantly: never bake local secrets (.env) or host build state
# (Windows node_modules, .next) into the image; the Dockerfile runs its own
# `npm ci` / `next build`, and compose supplies runtime config via `environment:`.
# The app's root-.env loader (next.config.ts) treats a missing file as a no-op,
# so the filtered context is safe for `next build` inside the image.

# secrets — never in the image
.env
.env.*
**/.env
**/.env.*

# dependencies & build output (installed/built inside the image)
node_modules
**/node_modules
**/.next
dist
build
coverage
.turbo
*.tsbuildinfo

# local runtime state (uploads, generated emails, sqlite experiments)
var
**/var
storage
**/storage
*.db
*.sqlite

# logs / OS / VCS / test artifacts
*.log
npm-debug.log*
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.git
playwright-report
test-results
